# Aethyme local-only activation. Deliberately outside the managed block above,
# because this is a repository *policy* choice rather than broker runtime state.
#
# `.aethyme/local/enabled` is the flag AGENTS.md checks, and `local/AGENTS.md` is
# the policy it points at. Committing either would make the full agent policy
# mandatory on every clone and every agent — which is the opposite of local-only
# mode, and would quietly change how the repository works for anyone who has not
# opted in. The shared parts (config.toml, gates.toml) are tracked on purpose, so
# sibling worktrees inherit the same gates.
#
# Each clone opts in once with: aethyme deploy --local-only --repo .
.aethyme/local/

# aethyme-broker:begin (managed block — do not edit inside)
.aethyme/broker.db*
.aethyme/logs/
.aethyme/reports/
.aethyme/run/
.aethyme/worktrees/
.aethyme/broker-action-required.md
.aethyme/broker-advisory.md
.aethyme/graph_store.redb
.aethyme/graph_store.redb.indexing
.aethyme/generated/experience-status.json
.aethyme/generated/experience-status.md
.aethyme/generated/experience-telemetry.jsonl
# aethyme-broker:end
